WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.281
A customer writes,

00:00:01.281 --> 00:00:05.617
“My payment never posted.” Is that a
card payment or a mortgage payment?

00:00:05.827 --> 00:00:08.061
A wrong transfer makes the customer wait

00:00:08.061 --> 00:00:10.295
while a second team reads the complaint.

00:00:10.505 --> 00:00:14.358
Relay recommends a desk
when the evidence is strong.

00:00:14.358 --> 00:00:15.643
Otherwise, staff decide.

00:00:16.123 --> 00:00:20.607
We trained on public Consumer
Financial Protection Bureau complaints.

00:00:20.817 --> 00:00:24.714
Relay reads the message, client
mailbox and state when known.

00:00:24.714 --> 00:00:28.222
Adding a transformer did not
improve the simpler model.

00:00:28.432 --> 00:00:31.548
Only cards and mortgages
passed our June checks.

00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:34.039
Try two fictional complaints.

00:00:34.249 --> 00:00:38.095
A customer disputes a
duplicate credit card charge.

00:00:38.095 --> 00:00:41.459
Relay scores the card desk at 99.2%.

00:00:41.669 --> 00:00:45.958
The desk passed its audit, so
Relay recommends a handoff.

00:00:46.438 --> 00:00:49.721
Now a collector keeps calling
about a debt already paid.

00:00:49.931 --> 00:00:56.111
Collections scores even higher,
at 99.9%, but failed its audit.

00:00:56.321 --> 00:00:59.143
A person still chooses the destination.

00:00:59.623 --> 00:01:06.014
We locked the rules in June, then
tested them on 8,830 July complaints.

00:01:06.224 --> 00:01:09.919
Relay recommended one desk for 928.

00:01:09.919 --> 00:01:14.231
Seventeen recommendations disagreed
with the recorded product:

00:01:14.231 --> 00:01:19.775
1.8% of recommendations, versus
12.5% with the historical rule.

00:01:19.985 --> 00:01:22.207
No customer was transferred.

00:01:22.687 --> 00:01:26.288
For cases kept by staff,
including short messages,

00:01:26.288 --> 00:01:28.538
we tested a two-desk shortlist.

00:01:28.748 --> 00:01:32.476
In July it included the recorded product 91%

00:01:32.476 --> 00:01:35.738
of the time, versus 63% with keywords.

00:01:35.948 --> 00:01:37.250
Does it save time?

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:38.878
That needs a live test.

00:01:39.358 --> 00:01:42.903
We recommend a pilot where
staff confirm every handoff.

00:01:43.113 --> 00:01:45.051
Audit 400 proposals per desk

00:01:45.051 --> 00:01:49.701
and randomly show or hide the
shortlist to measure time and accuracy.

00:01:49.911 --> 00:01:51.882
Under our cost assumptions,

00:01:51.882 --> 00:01:56.315
the July results imply $1,410
per 10,000 eligible complaints.

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:59.270
The pilot should test that estimate.
